 34S  c  J|p=3/2+ for {+35}Cl ground state (2026Su18).                          
 34S  c  1977Pa29: 14.1-MeV neutrons were produced via the {+3}H(d,n){+4}He     
 34S 2c  reaction at an average rate of 10{+9} neutrons per second into 4|p sr  
 34S 3c  from the Brown University neutron generator and impinged on a          
 34S 4c  6.71-mg/cm{+2}, 99.32%-enriched {+35}Cl target. Deuterons were detected
 34S 5c  using a time-of-flight counter telescope consisting of two proportional
 34S 6c  counters and a NaI(Tl) crystal. Measured |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced levels, 
 34S 7c  L-transfers, spectroscopic factors from finite-range DWUCK-DWBA        
 34S 8c  analysis of the measured |s(|q).                                       
 34S  c  1968Mi02: 35CL(N,D) using 14.4-MeV neutrons produced at the Ruder      
 34S 2c  Boskovic Institute in Zagreb. The target was 6.86-mg/cm{+2}, natural   
 34S 3c  PbCl{-2} deposited on a gold backing. Deuterons were detected using a  
 34S 4c  counter telescope system consisting of three CO{-2} gas proportional   
 34S 5c  counters and a CsI(Tl) scintillator. Measured |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced    
 34S 6c  levels, L-transfers, spectroscopic factors from zero-range DWBA and    
 34S 7c  Plane Wave Born Approximation (PWBA) analyses of the measured |s(|q).  
 34S  c  1967Fa10: 35CL(N,D) using 14.1-MeV neutrons produced at the Institute  
 34S 2c  of Physics of the University of Milan. The target was 3.77-mg/cm{+2}   
 34S 3c  natural C6Cl6 on a platinum backing. Deuterons were detected using a   
 34S 4c  |DE-E counter telescope. Measured |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced levels,        
 34S 5c  L-transfers, spectroscopic factors from DWBA analysis of the measured  
 34S 6c  |s(|q).                                                                
